  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\n- `assets/posts/sodick-wire.cps` now posts a Wire Contour with skim passes. Before, it refused each skimmed contour by name (#617, #538).\r\n  - The rough pass keeps its C word after T91, before the first move.\r\n  - Each skim's C word comes after the previous pass's return to the threading point, before the skim's first move. The wire stays threaded. The section has one T91 and one T90. The pass links stay G01.\r\n  - A note line names each skim and its condition.\r\n  - A skim condition id that is not `C` and three digits is refused by name. The app writes no file.\r\n- New boolean post option `approachCondition` (default off). When it is on, the post writes `C000` before the first approach move (threading point to the contour). The operation's C word follows that move. Skims get no C000.\r\n- With the option off, the output for a contour without skims is byte-identical. The #617 goldens do not change.\r\n- `assets/posts/AGENTS.md`: the sodick-wire paragraph describes the skims and the option.\r\n- Decision entry: `docs/decisions/2649-sodick-ln-pass-structure.md`.\r\n\r\n## Reproduction\r\n\r\nOn `main` (370d38df6), a punch with the rough condition C001 and the skims C002 and C903 does not post through the Sodick post. The post refuses with \"a condition change between passes (skims) is not supported by this post\". So no LN1W / LN2W 2- or 3-pass job can post.\r\n\r\n## Sources\r\n\r\n- Sodick Inc., \"Wire EDM Machine Operation Training, LN1W / LN2W Control\" (AQ400L, AQ600L, AD360L; part number 6300015, January 2012), public at fab.cba.mit.edu/content/tools/sodick_edm/sodick_user_manual_small.pdf. We used behaviour only, and we copied no text and no sample program:\r\n  - the word list: C001 for the first cut, C002 for the second cut, C903 for the third cut;\r\n  - the NC program example: the next pass's C word after the return to the start point, with the wire left threaded;\r\n  - the condition header rows: C000 / H000 are named \"Approach\".\r\n- The existing #617 source (Sodick 1998 \"Wire EDM Machine Operation\", Mark 21 / EX21) for all other words.\r\n\r\n## Inferred, not stated by the source\r\n\r\n- The placement of C000. The manual names the row \"Approach\" but shows no program line with it. For this reason, the option is off by default and applies only to the first approach move.\r\n- Flushing for skims. The manual's example changes the flushing for the finish passes. The post writes no flushing word for a skim. Follow-up: #2686.\r\n\r\n## Readings (new golden `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sodick-wire/wire_slug_punch_passes.nc`)\r\n\r\n- `T91`, then `C001`, then the rough lead-in `G01 X-20.165 Y0.`.\r\n- After the return `G01 X-30. Y0.`: `(SKIM 1 ...)`, `C002`, then the lead-in `G01 X-20.145 Y0.`.\r\n- After the next return: `(SKIM 2 ...)`, `C903`, then the reversed pass from `G01 X-20.135 Y0.`.\r\n- `T90`, `M02`. There is no `G00` between T91 and T90.\r\n- The skim lead-ins match the wire-iso skims golden (`wire_contour_punch_skims.nc`).\r\n\r\n## Pinning tests\r\n\r\n- `sodick_wire_passes::a_rough_cut_and_two_skims_post_each_pass_on_its_own_ln_condition` - ok\r\n- `sodick_wire_passes::the_approach_condition_option_cuts_the_first_approach_on_c000` - ok\r\n- `sodick_wire_passes::a_skim_condition_that_is_not_a_sodick_c_word_is_refused_by_name` - ok\r\n- `sodick_wire_post` (8 tests, the #617 golden unchanged) - ok\r\n- Removed: `sodick_wire_post::skims_are_refused_by_name_never_cut_on_the_rough_condition`. Skims now post, and the new file pins them.\r\n\r\n## Golden changes\r\n\r\n- New: `wire_slug_punch_passes.nc`.\r\n- Changed: none. `wire_slug_punch.nc` and `wire_slug_punch_flushed.nc` stay byte-identical.\r\n\r\n## Gate\r\n\r\nQuick gate on e7bda5b1f (334eacd3a with `git merge origin/main` at 5c39bff51, no conflict): `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`, 589 steps, 0 failed, wall 56.4 min.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- The output was not run on a Sodick LN1W / LN2W control.\r\n- The `approachCondition` option through the post dialog UI (the host renders declared options; tested through the engine only).\r\n- Skims combined with `edm.flushing` / `edm.tank`, and skims without automatic threading (no new code path for these).\r\n\r\nChangelog: Sodick wire post: skim passes now post on their own LN condition words (C001 / C002 / C903), and a new option cuts the approach move on C000.\r\n\r\nEffort: high\r\n\r\nFixes #2649\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n\r\n",
